": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "1006 and 1860 are connected statically and even by an unconstrained time-respecting walk, but that walk requires waits up to 9109 units between hops. Under the 600-unit relay constraint (and even at 1500) 1006's temporal forward set is only 8 nodes and excludes 1860, and no path is enumerable. The apparent link is an artefact of dense static connectivity and high background activity, not a genuine cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "**Conclusion**\n\n- With the required \u2264600-unit gap, node 1006 reaches only 8 nodes in [18031, 56431] and 1860 is not among them (step_01); no time-respecting route exists (step_11).\n- A connection does exist when the delay constraint is relaxed: an unconstrained temporal path 1006\u219245\u219225\u2192156\u21921243\u21921028\u2192943\u21921776\u2192153\u21921860 exists, but its inter-hop waits are 372, 4961, 217, 2873, 2104, 1930, 1025, 9109 \u2014 up to ~15\u00d7 the allowed budget (step_03).\n- Even loosening the constraint to 1500 units still fails (step_08), so the failure is not a knife-edge threshold effect.\n- Confounders ruled out: the window is busy overall (7200 events, 1941 active nodes, step_02) and 1006/1860 sit in a large, densely connected static 2-hop neighbourhood (step_04); both endpoints are low-degree (5 events each, step_05) with activity in largely non-overlapping bins (step_09, step_10), and their out/in contact sets are disjoint (step_06, step_07). So static connectivity and background volume \u2014 not timing \u2014 explain any apparent link.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_636b848d\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1006, 1860],\n  \"window\": [18031, 56431],\n  \"confidence\": 0.88,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1006 and 1860 are connected statically and even by an unconstrained time-respecting walk, but that walk requires waits up to 9109 units between hops. Under the 600-unit relay constraint (and even at 1500) 1006's temporal forward set is only 8 nodes and excludes 1860, and no path is enumerable. The apparent link is an artefact of dense static connectivity and high background activity, not a genuine cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 32852, "total_output_tokens": 2706, "total_tokens": 35558, "total_latency_ms": 43224, "llm_calls": 5, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}